From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:40:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] kk: Give 2D and 2D array views a texture of the other
 type

D3D12 applications bind 2D array views to Texture2D declarations and the
other way round. Unreal Engine 5 writes its TSR output to a one-layer 2D
array and reads it as a 2D texture for bloom and tonemapping. Other APIs
read such a view as its first layer. Metal reads garbage from a texture
whose type differs from the argument's declared type: every coordinate
returned the same texel, so with Direct3D 12 the whole screen was one
colour.

Sampled 2D and 2D array views now also create a Metal view of the other
type, a 2D view of the first layer for 2D arrays. Sampled image
descriptors carry the 2D texture in image_gpu_resource_id and the 2D
array texture in a new image_array_gpu_resource_id, taken from padding,
and texture2d_array declarations load the latter.

Town To City (Unreal Engine 5.7) with Direct3D 12 renders its world
instead of a flat colour.

Generated-by: LLM
